<p>I'm impressed at how you were able to make a simple humanoid anomaly so effective. That said, a couple things are holding me back from an upvote. His dialogue in the interview comes in big, expository blocks, and it often feels like he's narrating a story, like, <em>written</em> narration, not spoken, not from memory.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Further study into SCP-3619's anatomy is severely hampered by the fact that non-euclidean spaces are, by definition, incomprehensible to human beings.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Also, this doesn't quite seem right. I mean, even putting aside &quot;the Foundation contains a lot of non-Euclidean anomalies&quot;, it would just be simpler to cut it off at &quot;hampered&quot; (with a &quot;has been&quot;, of course), there's no need to explain why.</p>

